-- `l4 batch` prints the checked module back and checks it again next to a
-- generated record that has a field for each input. If the printer wrote this
-- annotation back, `%a%` would have two candidates, the input and the field,
-- and no expected type to choose between them; the checker refuses that
-- ("multiple definitions") and every row would be an `error`. The printer
-- writes no annotation back, so the row runs.

@export Whether the amount is large
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is large` @nlg the amount %a% is large
  IF a GREATER THAN 100
